Changes made in Iris (see git history for details):
- Private mode: every command, message and button is limited to the owner and an allow list;
  access managed from the bot with one-time invite links, /adduser, /deluser, /users and
  Allow/Deny notifications
- Russian user interface: texts, progress bar, statuses, settings menu, error messages, command menu
- Quality setting and full titles for VK, OK.ru and other non-YouTube sites
- Instagram photo posts and carousels sent as albums; files sent by their real type
  (video, photo, audio, document); albums over 10 items split
- Downloads deleted as soon as a job ends; hourly sweep of leftovers; uploads retried without
  resending delivered album parts; progress updated every 1.5 s and removed when done
- Egress firewall that blocks the home network, tailnet and Docker host (SSRF protection),
  fail-closed, with the bot process running without NET_ADMIN
- yt-dlp nightly with automatic daily updates inside the container
- Single-container setup: SQLite and in-memory cache instead of MySQL and Redis
- Tests, CI, bilingual documentation, new name, logo and banner
- Removed upstream donation, deployment and Docker Hub publishing files
